From: Tamizh Chelvam Raja <tamizhr@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Mon, 26 May 2025 18:29:55 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: offload AP VLAN WDS peers to PPE

AP_VLAN interfaces do not own firmware vdevs, but a four-address WDS
station still needs a distinct PPE virtual port.  Sending all such peers
through the parent AP virtual port loses the downstream peer selection and
keeps bridged traffic on the software path.

Allocate a direct-switch VP for each four-address AP_VLAN while reusing the
parent AP firmware vdev, PMAC and bank in the hardware profile.  Move both
the MLD and link peer mappings between the parent and VLAN VP from the
sta_set_4addr callback, and use the parent vdev for firmware station state.

Keep non-four-address AP_VLAN interfaces on the software path.  Preserve
the logical parent and peer relationship across channel changes and
firmware recovery, while invalidating hardware VP state before the PPE
datapath is rebuilt.

Based-on: ba31901cc92e3aa4aa2799876745af447b8a8bae
Link: https://git.codelinaro.org/clo/qsdk/oss/system/feeds/wlan-open/-/blob/1ee3a4ab7c59ceaff347c4668fc6c7604a04c323/patches/ath12k/0337-10-QSDK-DP-wifi-Enable-DS-support-for-WDS-AP_VLAN-inter.patch
Signed-off-by: Tamizh Chelvam Raja <tamizhr@qti.qualcomm.com>
Signed-off-by: Balamurugan Mahalingam <bmahalin@qti.qualcomm.com>
Assisted-by: Codex:GPT-5.6-sol
Signed-off-by: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
